{"availability":"available","full":"zSamir015/drafty","name":"drafty","description":"Kanban board with a blueprint, pointer-based drag & drop and Motion animations. Vanilla JS, no build, offline PWA.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-09T03:54:54Z","updated":"2026-10-11T03:41:05Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://zsamir015.github.io/drafty/","topics":["animation","drag-and-drop","javascript","kanban","motion","portfolio","pwa","vanilla-js"],"demo":"https://zsamir015.github.io/drafty/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:06.539Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:06.539Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:06.539Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:06.539Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Drafty is a Kanban board styled like a technical drawing. It is written in plain JavaScript with no framework and no build step, and the interface is in Spanish.","The interesting part is the interaction layer: drag and drop is built on pointer events instead of the HTML5 drag API, the board re-renders by reconciling keyed nodes, and every change goes through one function that records history, saves and redraws. All of it works with the keyboard and offline."],"features":["Three columns (to do, in progress, done) and several boards in tabs. Boards can be created, renamed with a double click and deleted.","Cards with a title, priority, label and due date. Overdue cards are flagged.","Drag and drop with mouse or touch (long press on touch). Esc cancels a drag, and the page scrolls when you drag near the top or bottom edge.","Undo and redo with Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+Shift+Z, up to 100 steps. Deleting a card also shows an \"Undo\" toast.","Live search by title, label or card code (for example TK-007)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/zSamir015/drafty/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"83fb903ee79a4cf260d83796cc2968a2d6d8a7eda45d